+Environment-prefill variables for Aegis production bootstrap
+
+Before running the automated bootstrap or the one-click PoA harness, export these environment variables with values for your environment.
+
+Required environment variables (example values):
+
+- CLUSTER_CONTEXT="arn:aws:eks:us-west-2:123456789012:cluster/aegis-prod"   # kubectl/helm context name
+- REGISTRY="123456789012.dkr.ecr.us-west-2.amazonaws.com/aegis"           # container registry
+- COSIGN_KMS_URI="awskms://alias/aegis-cosign-key"                       # cosign KMS URI (or gcpkms:/, azure)
+- REKOR_SERVER="https://rekor.example.com"                               # Rekor transparency server
+- S3_UPLOAD="s3://aegis-evidence"                                        # S3 bucket for evidence & audit
+- REDIS_URL="redis://redis.aegis.svc:6379/0"                             # session store
+- OIDC_ISSUER_URL="https://login.example.com"                            # OIDC issuer for SSO
+- OIDC_CLIENT_ID="aegis-client-id"                                       # OIDC client ID
+- OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET="<redacted>"                                        # OIDC client secret (use Vault)
+- PROMPT_REGISTRY_HELM_VALUES="/tmp/prompt_values.yaml"                  # optional helm values file
+
+Optional / tuning variables:
+- NUM_DEEPSPEED_NODES=2
+- GPUS_PER_NODE=8
+- TRITON_REPLICAS=1
+- VLLM_REPLICAS=1
+
+Security notes:
+- Never put secrets in git. Place OIDC secrets and COSIGN_KMS_URIs into Vault or GitHub secrets, and reference them via the bootstrap (scripts read from environment or Vault).
+
